I've been playing nethack quite a lot at work lately (if you don't
have your +2 TSR of stealth yet, ask me for one today..for real!),
and I've noticed some curious things.

1. When I am invisible, and first set foot in a shop, the shopkeeper says
"Invisible customers are not welcome", and he won't budge from the door.
Even if I enter from a hole I made in the side with a wand of digging, he
still blocks his doorway.  Then, when I walk in anyway, he acts like nothing's
wrong.  When I pick something up, he says "for you, good sir..." and all
that.  So I'm not welcome but he doesn't get mad when I break in.

2. I had on a ring of warning (uncursed, unknown enchantment) for quite some
time and it did nothing, even during battles.

3. g<dir> quit working.  It always moves exactly one space now.  Could it
be a minor bug having to do with being invisible?  or being quick?

4. Bats don't care about Elbereth.  Is that because they're blind as a bat?

5. I killed a cockatrice and kept the corpse, figuring I could wield it
if I got into trouble.  Not wanting to touch it carelessly, I put it in
my bag.  Later, when I went to take it out, everything seemed fine:
Do you want to take something out? y [...] (i) a cockatrice corpse
Great!  But immediately I did an inventory and it had vanished.  I mean it.
I think that is definitely a bug.

6. I dipped a spellbook into a fountain and felt a feeling of loss.  Does that
mean it used to be blessed, and is now only uncursed?

7. I've seen it suggested repeatedly that it's a good idea to have twice
the level in terms of experience than the dungeon level you're on.  I've
always ended up playing just about one for one, yet I think I'm pretty
thorough clearing levels.

8. I used a wand of make invisible to zap myself, and I love being invisible.
When I found I was carrying too much stuff, I discarded two wands of make
invisible.  Is there anything else useful that I can do with them?  Could
anything happen to make me lose my invisibility, so I would want the wand
again?

9. I was careless enough to eat a nymph and started feeling jumpy.  It hasn't
really upset my game much, but I noticed that sometimes I jump several
times in just a few turns, and other times I'll go quite a long time without
teleporting.  Is this just random, or does it depend on something?
If I somehow get teleport control, then will I be asked where I want to go
when I get jumpy?

10. What all can you do without scuffing an engraving?  I know if you hit
or throw, it gets messed up.  Can you zap a wand or cast a spell?

11. Can you offer a tin, or must it be fresh meat?

12. I dipped some scrolls in a fountain, figuring I'd roll my own with my
magic (tm) marker (46).  Alas, when I went to write, it said, "In your
haste, you rip the scroll to shreds".  I tried again, this time waiting
what I thought was quite a long time, and it still tore the scroll.  Do you
need fire or something to dry the scrolls, or do you just have to wait a
very long time?


Well, that's enough ramblings for now!

